## Abstract

In this thesis we present a new method for the calculation of the \(\pi^{0}\)-meson decay width in the \(\pi^{0}\)-decay region. We show that the \(\pi^{0}\)-meson decay width is enhanced by about 1% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV, and that the \(\pi^{0}\)-meson width is enhanced by about 3% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV. The \(\pi^{0}\)-meson width is enhanced by about 5% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV, and the \(\pi^{0}\)-meson width is enhanced by about 4% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV. The \(\pi^{0}\)-meson width is enhanced by about 6% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV, and the \(\pi^{0}\)-meson width is enhanced by about 7% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV. The \(\pi^{0}\)-meson width is enhanced by about 8% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV, and the \(\pi^{0}\)-meson width is enhanced by about 9% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV. The \(\pi^{0}\)-meson width is enhanced by about 1% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV, and the \(\pi^{0}\)-meson width is enhanced by about 1% at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) MeV.



